0058:     """
0059:     Keep the largest 8-connected motif and replace the corner/control pixels with a solid corner triangle.
0060: 
0061:     Input structure
0062:     - The background is the dominant color.
0063:     - Exactly one grid corner contains a foreground control pixel; it gives the
0064:       corner from which the triangle is painted.
0065:     - There is one unique largest 8-connected monochrome foreground object, the
0066:       motif that remains in the output; all other foreground pixels are controls.
0067:     - Every foreground component outside that motif is a singleton control pixel.
0068:     - The fill color is the unique control color that appears in at least two
0069:       non-corner control pixels.
0070: 
0071:     Rule
0072:     - Start from a blank background canvas and redraw only the largest motif.
0073:     - Count the non-corner control pixels; that count is the triangle side.
0074:     - Paint the fill color on the right-triangle region where those two distances
0075:       from the marked corner's edges sum to less than the side length.
0076: 
0077:     Key insight
0078:     - The scattered singleton controls are counted into a compact triangular
0079:       stack at the marked corner; only the largest motif is not part of the count.
